S"Anne runs for re-election to the town council, shepherded by Matthieu, her fellow candidate and campaign manager. Her husband, G\xc3\xa9rard, a businessman and philanderer, hates the campaign and feels vindication when a nasty leaflet circulates about their family history. His son, Fran\xc3\xa7ois, just back from the U.S., is in love with his step-sister Mich\xc3\xa8le, and she with him, although something is amiss besides their being cousins. Watching it all is their elderly Aunt Line, who has her own haunting memories. A death in World War II and a death on election night collapse time in the perpetual present and bring unexpected expiation. There's a lot to celebrate."
