S'A zombie pandemic erupts in major cities around the world; those bitten by the creatures become zombies themselves within 12 seconds. Retired UN investigator Gerry Lane, his wife Karin, and their two daughters escape the outbreak in Philadelphia and travel to Newark, where they take shelter with another family. Gerry\'s friend, UN Deputy Secretary-General Umuntoni, arranges their rescue. When their U.S. Air Force helicopter arrives, zombies invade the house and their hosts are bitten, with only their son managing to escape with the Lanes. They are flown to a Navy carrier group offshore New York City. The onboard scientists, needing to find patient zero, focus on Camp Humphreys in South Korea \xe2\x80\x93 thought to be the source of their first known mention of "zombie". A team of Navy SEALs is dispatched with Dr. Fassbach, a virologist. Gerry is coerced into going with them, or risk having his family sent to a potentially unsafe refugee camp. When the team\'s plane lands at Camp Humphreys, they are ambushed by zombies and Fassbach accidentally shoots himself dead. Inside the compound, Gerry learns that a South Korean doctor was the first to come down with the zombie infection, turning about 10 minutes after being bitten by a soldier who had been somewhat deranged for days. He also learns that an injured soldier had not been attacked when surrounded by zombies. A disgraced CIA operative, held at the base for selling arms to North Korea, reveals that North Korea understood the threat before it occurred and had already pulled the teeth of all 23 million citizens, while Israel had reacted a week before the outbreak, reinforcing their historically walled cities. He directs Gerry to Jerusalem and Mossad agent Warmbrunn. In Jerusalem, Warmbrunn reveals they had intercepted a message that the Indian Army was fighting the rakshasa ("demon"). He and other Israeli experts convinced the government to close their cities to protect themselves. As Gerry is escorted back to his plane by the IDF, zombies are drawn by loud music and singing in the city and they pile up against the wall and are able to enter the city. As the city is quickly overtaken, Gerry and his IDF escorts battle their way to the airport. During the way, Gerry notices an old man and a young feeble boy are ignored by the zombies. A zombie bites the hand of Gerry\'s IDF escort, who refuses to reveal her name and asks him to call her "Segen"(Hebrew for Lieutenant). Gerry swiftly amputates her hand to prevent her turning. The group reaches the airport, but by the time they arrive, Gerry\'s pilot had ditched him. The escort group stops a plane about to leave, and they allow Gerry and Segen to board; the rest of the group stays behind. On the plane, Gerry contacts Umuntoni, who directs the pilots to a WHO facility in Cardiff. As the plane nears Cardiff, a zombie is discovered on the plane, and most of the passengers are quickly bitten and infected. Having no other choice, Gerry throws a grenade to rupture the cabin and eject the zombies, but it also causes the plane to crash land. Gerry and Segen are the only survivors, though Gerry is impaled on some debris. As they reach the WHO facility, Gerry passes out and falls in a coma. Gerry wakes up three days later. He is unable to convince the scientists of his identity, so he contacts Umuntoni. Umuntoni convinces the scientists, but tells Gerry his family was shipped to the mainland. Gerry explains his theory that the zombies need a healthy host to carry the infection. Gerry suggests injecting himself with a deadly, but curable disease that acts as a camouflage and makes him appear invisible from the zombies. The WHO scientists agree, but point out that the pathogens are located in a zombie-infested area of the lab. Gerry, Segen, and a scientist infiltrate the lab, but zombies spot them. Segen and the scientist make it to safety, while Gerry finds himself in a room with the pathogens. As he attempts to leave, a lone zombie blocks his escape route. Gerry injects himself and proves his hypothesis is correct when the zombie ignores him. Gerry, carrying the pathogens, safely bypasses other zombies. Later, Gerry and Segen are taken to a Nova Scotia refugee camp where Gerry is reunited with his family. Gerry explains there is a vaccine that is a hybridized mix of meningitis, smallpox and H1N1 that camouflages humans from zombies and allows them to safely travel through zombie hordes and mount attacks against them. The zombies are in an area and stand dormant when no un-vaccinated humans or loud noises are present. Gerry states that the war against the zombies is just beginning. Mexico City is devastated by the zombies. Paris is overrun and burning, while the residents of Moscow fight the zombies for control of the city.'
