S'The film follows the story of Otilia Mihartescu (Anamaria Marinca) and Gabriela "G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba" Dragut (Laura Vasiliu), two university friends in an unnamed Romanian town. The film is set in 1987, one of the last years of the Ceau\xc8\x99escu government. When G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba becomes pregnant, the two girls arrange a meeting with Mr. Bebe (Vlad Ivanov) in a hotel, where he is to perform an illegal abortion (Communist Romania had a natalist policy against abortion). At the college dorm G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba and Otilia review the items they need for the day, and as G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba nervously sits and waits in the room, Otilia barters and buys soap, cigarettes, etc. from school friends. Afterwards, Otilia takes a bus to visit her boyfriend Adi, from whom she borrows money. Adi asks Otilia to visit his family that night, as it is his mother\'s birthday, and to buy flowers on the way, to which Otilia initially declines, but she relents after Adi becomes upset. Otilia heads to a hotel where G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba has booked a room, only to be informed by an unfriendly receptionist that there is no reservation under G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba\'s last name. Otilia goes to another hotel, and after much begging and haggling is able to book a room at an expensive rate. Afterwards Otilia goes to a rendezvous point to meet with Mr. Bebe, although he had asked G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba that she meets him and no one else. Mr. Bebe grows angry upon hearing that G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba is not at the planned hotel. Mr. Bebe discovers that G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba\'s claim that her pregnancy was in its third month is a lie; in fact, it has been at least four months. The two women were certain that they would pay no more than 3000 lei for the abortion. However, it slowly becomes clear to the women that he expects both women to have sex with him. Otilia reluctantly has sex with Mr. Bebe so that he will not walk out on them, and eventually G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba does as well. Mr. Bebe then performs the abortion by injecting a probe and an unnamed fluid into G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba\'s uterus, and leaves Otilia instructions on how to dispose of the fetus when it comes out. Otilia is exasperated by G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba\'s lies, yet continues to help her and care for her. Otilia leaves G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba at the hotel to go to Adi\'s mother\'s birthday. She is still disturbed but stays and has dinner with Adi\'s mother\'s friends, who are mostly doctors. They all talk about trivial things while Otilia and Adi remain silent. The phone rings in the background, but no one answers it. One of the guests then starts talking about lost values and respect to elders when Otilia accepts a cigarette offered to her in front of Adi\'s parents, which prompts Adi to bring the champagne in order to get the party over with. Adi and Otilia then go to his room where Otilia tells him about G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba\'s abortion, and they start talking about what would happen if it was Otilia who was pregnant since Adi seems to be against abortion. After fighting with Adi, Otilia calls G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba from Adi\'s house. G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba does not answer, so Otilia decides to go back to G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba. When Otilia enters the room G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba is lying on the bed, and she tells Otilia that the fetus has come out and is in the bathroom. Otilia then wraps the fetus with some towels and puts everything in a bag, while G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba asks her to bury the fetus. Otilia then goes outside and walks around for a while, finally climbing to the top of a random building, as Mr. Bebe had suggested, and dropping the bag in a trash chute. Otilia then goes back to the hotel and finds G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba sitting at the restaurant. She sits and tells G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba that they are never going to talk about the episode ever again. Otilia stares blankly at G\xc4\x83bi\xc8\x9ba before looking directly at the camera, letting the audience decide what will happen between the two friends, just before the film cuts to black.'
