S"The film begins with an introductory sequence involving the main characters and images from space and introducing many of the film's visual leitmotifs. These are motifs of virtually still images revealing the key elements of the film: Justine the bride in deep melancholy with birds falling behind her; of a lawn with trees and sundial with two different shadows; Pieter Breughel's The Hunters in the Snow (often used as interpretation of an idealised nostalgia) burning; the nonexistent 19th hole, and the Black Horse collapsing catastrophically in slow motion; Justine as a bride being swept along by a river; and her being held back by her wedding dress; and finally Justine and her nephew building their magic cave before Melancholia crashes into Earth."
