S"In 1975 Spain, a young girl named Laura is adopted. Years later, adult Laura (Rueda) returns to the closed orphanage, accompanied by her husband, Carlos (Cayo), and their seven-year-old son, Sim\xc3\xb3n (Pr\xc3\xadncep). She plans to reopen the orphanage as a facility for disabled children. Sim\xc3\xb3n claims to have befriended a boy named Tom\xc3\xa1s, and draws pictures of him as a child wearing a sack mask. Social worker Benigna Escobedo (Montserrat Carulla) visits the house to inquire after Sim\xc3\xb3n, and the audience learn that Laura and Carlos adopted Sim\xc3\xb3n and that he is HIV positive. Incensed at Benigna's intrusion, Laura asks her to leave. Later that night Laura finds Benigna in the orphanage's coal shed, but Benigna flees the scene. Later, Sim\xc3\xb3n teaches Laura a game which grants its winner a wish. Clues lead the two to Sim\xc3\xb3n's adoption file. Sim\xc3\xb3n becomes angry, and says that his new friend told him that Laura is not his biological mother and that he is going to die soon. During a party for the orphanage's opening, Laura and Sim\xc3\xb3n argue, and Sim\xc3\xb3n hides from her. While looking for him, she encounters a child wearing a sack mask who shoves her into a bathroom and locks her inside. Escaping, she finds that Sim\xc3\xb3n is missing; she is unable to find him. That night Laura hears several loud crashes within the walls of the orphanage. Police psychologist Pilar (Mabel Rivera) suggests to Laura and Carlos that Benigna may have abducted Sim\xc3\xb3n. Six months later, Sim\xc3\xb3n is still missing. While searching for him, Laura spots Benigna, who is then struck and killed by a car. The police find evidence that Benigna worked at the orphanage, and that she had a son named Tom\xc3\xa1s, who lived there but was kept hidden. A few weeks after Laura was adopted, the orphans stole the mask that Tom\xc3\xa1s wore to conceal his deformed face. Embarrassed, Tom\xc3\xa1s refused to leave his hiding place in a nearby sea cave, and the rising tide drowned him. Laura asks for the assistance of a medium named Aurora (Geraldine Chaplin) in the search for Sim\xc3\xb3n. Aurora conducts a seance during which she claims to see the ghosts of the orphans crying for help. Laura discovers the remains of the orphans she grew up with in the orphanage. Benigna poisoned their meals and killed them for having caused Tom\xc3\xa1s's death and hid their remains in the orphanage's coal shed. Unable to cope with the situation, Carlos leaves the orphanage. Laura makes the orphanage look as it did thirty years ago and attempts to contact the children's spirits by playing one of their old games. The spirits lead her to the door of a hidden underground room. Inside is Sim\xc3\xb3n's corpse, wearing Tom\xc3\xa1s's mask. Laura finally realizes what happened: while searching for Sim\xc3\xb3n the night he disappeared, Laura moved pieces of construction scaffolding, blocking the entrance to the secret room. The crashes that night were caused by Sim\xc3\xb3n trying to get out. He fell and broke his neck. Laura takes an overdose of sleeping pills. Dying, she begs to be with Sim\xc3\xb3n again and the children's spirits appear, with Sim\xc3\xb3n among them. Sim\xc3\xb3n tells Laura that his wish was for her to stay and take care of the orphans, she then happily tells them a story. Sometime later, Carlos visits a memorial to Laura, Sim\xc3\xb3n and the orphans. Carlos returns to the orphans' old bedroom and finds a medallion that he had given to Laura. He turns to look as the door opens, and he smiles."
