S'Set in 1900s Belle \xc3\x89poque Paris, Ch\xc3\xa9ri  tells the story of the end of a six-year affair between an aging retired courtesan, L\xc3\xa9a, and a flamboyant young man, Fred, nicknamed "Ch\xc3\xa9ri" . Although L\xc3\xa9a only plans on keeping Ch\xc3\xa9ri around for a short while, their affair turns into a six-year ordeal, in which L\xc3\xa9a has begun paying for Ch\xc3\xa9ri\'s expenses, and Ch\xc3\xa9ri wears L\xc3\xa9a\'s silk pajamas and pearls. The two believe their affair to be casual, and L\xc3\xa9a learns from Charlotte that she has arranged for Ch\xc3\xa9ri to marry the daughter of another courtesan, a barely eighteen-year-old named Edm\xc3\xa9e. Although Ch\xc3\xa9ri does not wish to marry Edm\xc3\xa9e, it is made clear that he has no choice in the matter. L\xc3\xa9a kicks him out of her home, but makes Ch\xc3\xa9ri promise to always be gentle and kind with Edm\xc3\xa9e, and to try and give her a good life. After Ch\xc3\xa9ri agrees, the two part ways, and do not share glances at Ch\xc3\xa9ri\'s wedding. It is only after Ch\xc3\xa9ri is on the train to Italy for his honeymoon that both he and L\xc3\xa9a realize they are in love with each other. Ch\xc3\xa9ri rapes Edm\xc3\xa9e and, while taking her virginity, realizes that while sex with Edm\xc3\xa9e is strained and painful, sex with L\xc3\xa9a was easy and fun. L\xc3\xa9a visits Charlotte one last time before running off on vacation, making up a story in which she is involved in with another suitor, when in fact the only man L\xc3\xa9a beds while on vacation is a young bodybuilder whom she has no feelings for and regards as a one-night-stand. Meanwhile, Edm\xc3\xa9e accuses Ch\xc3\xa9ri of not caring about her, and says all he ever does is think of L\xc3\xa9a. While out on the town with a friend, Ch\xc3\xa9ri tries opium and cocaine, and on his way back he notices that L\xc3\xa9a\'s apartment is no longer empty, and she has returned home. Feeling refreshed, Ch\xc3\xa9ri runs home to Edm\xc3\xa9e where he makes love to her properly and kindly. He sends Charlotte the next day to inspect L\xc3\xa9a\'s home, whereupon L\xc3\xa9a says she is madly in love with her new "suitor", and learns  from Charlotte that Ch\xc3\xa9ri and Edm\xc3\xa9e are crazily in love and happier than ever. That night, after hearing from Charlotte that L\xc3\xa9a is in love with her suitor, Ch\xc3\xa9ri breaks into her home and admits he loves her. The two spend one more night together and plan on running away. In the morning, however, L\xc3\xa9a apologizes to Ch\xc3\xa9ri for "ruining him" and making life too easy on him when they first begun their affair. L\xc3\xa9a tells Ch\xc3\xa9ri to go back to Edm\xc3\xa9e, for their age difference would always prevent a true relationship blossoming between them. Tentatively, Ch\xc3\xa9ri leaves. L\xc3\xa9a stares into her mirror at her aging face, and the narrator reveals she is angry for being born two decades before Ch\xc3\xa9ri. The narrator also reveals that, after a while, Ch\xc3\xa9ri realizes that L\xc3\xa9a was the only woman he could ever love, and he commits suicide.'
